{"author":{"id":"f943aa1c5ee078b881a8e97535a4e2ccb401d01ca00f4128126befa9cca58a32"},"ops":[{"type":6,"timestamp":1792680244,"nonce":"MS+h1TghCr/ztqpLqFlFuc7fpSY=","target":"126afe155f8d23cb1165461d29850f3f7fb6dd2ae2a055bca4c01dcec04810de","message":"The live test of #31 (native fields: kinds as GitHub issue types, v0.11.1-sync.9) found two defects in the fork. The test ran on guilbep-sandbox/native-fields-test on 2026-10-21; its results are on #31.\n\n1. **A kind swap takes two syncs.** On an issue with type Bug and the label `feat`, removing `bug` and syncing removes type Bug but leaves `feat` as a label. The next sync removes the label and sets type Feature. One sync should do both.\n2. **The echo of a type move isn't recognized.** When a push moves `bug` from a label to the type, the next sync's pull writes two label ops, `-bug` and `+bug`, on the git-bug side. The labels end up the same and nothing goes to GitHub, but each round writes them again until it settles. The SetMetadata commits after a push are the same in sync.8: leave them alone.\n\nThe work happens in a worktree of the fork off `bridge-sync`. Start with `doc/design/bridges/native-fields.md` and `sync-decisions.md`, then the GitHub adapter's type handling.\n\n\n- Each defect has a test with the GitHub fake that fails before the fix.\n- The live test passes checks 1 to 6 and 8 on guilbep-sandbox/native-fields-test. Live tests run there only.\n- `native-fields.md` says where the live test ran and what it found.\n- Once the user tags sync.10, git-board's go.mod pins it, and #31 reruns its live test and closes.\n- Then v0.10.1 is cut from the Releases page (v0.10.0 shipped sync.9 on 2026-10-22).","files":null}]}